# Shell scripts must stay LF in the working tree, on every platform. This repo runs with
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out text to CRLF on Windows — and a hook whose
# shebang reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` dies with "bad interpreter", which is how the failure
# presents: not as a syntax error, as a file that cannot be executed at all.
#
# This became load-bearing when .claude/hooks/ started being tracked: those seven scripts are
# LF on disk today, and without this line the first fresh checkout or worktree would receive
# them as CRLF and every hook would silently stop running.
*.sh text eol=lf
